  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe upward bias during high-volatility regimes; when recent history shows a sharp spike (e.g., >80), the model fails to capture the subsequent mean-reversion and instead predicts a slow, linear climb.",
    "The model systematically underestimates the magnitude of immediate post-spike corrections, assuming volatility will dampen quickly rather than triggering a rapid drop back to historical averages.",
    "Sentiment history (values >0.25) correlates with higher forecast errors; positive sentiment signals appear to be ignored by the model, leading to over-optimistic trajectories during periods of actual market stress.",
    "The 30-day horizon is structurally flawed for this asset class; the model predicts a smooth trend while true outcomes display erratic, non-linear swings that invalidate linear extrapolation.",
    "When the last 5 days show a rising trend followed by a spike, the model should apply a negative correction factor to the forecasted path to account for expected mean reversion."
  ]
}
